# Your Georgia Tech servers, in standard OpenSSH config syntax (the same
# format as ~/.ssh/config; see `man ssh_config`).
#
# Every "Host <name>" you add here:
#   - works inside the container as      ssh <name>
#     (X11 for Cadence/Vivado, compression and one Duo prompt per 8 hours
#     are on by default; set an option here to override it)
#   - appears in VS Code's Remote-SSH host list as   gt-<name>
#     (VS Code connects to that server through the container's tunnel)
#
# After editing, run:   gtvpn hosts
#
# HostName, User and Port carry over to VS Code. Keep other options to the
# ones you need inside the container. If you leave out User, GTVPN_GT_USER
# from .env is used for GT hosts.

# Host cadence
#     HostName ece-xxxx.ece.gatech.edu
#     User gburdell3
#
# Host pace
#     HostName login-ice.pace.gatech.edu
#
# Host lab-fpga
#     HostName 10.10.20.30
#     Port 2222
